          "before": "In the paraxial imaging model shown, rays from $A$ that reflect from the mirror pass through the image point $A_1$.\nChoose **any two** of the convenient rays to locate $A_1$.\nThe other reflected rays pass through the same image point.\n\nA real mirror may not reflect every convenient ray.\nFor example, some medical concave mirrors have a hole at the center, so a ray reaching the hole is not reflected.\nThe image can still be constructed using rays reflected by the remaining reflecting surface.",
